# Vercel uses THIS file (not .gitignore) to decide what to upload. Because the
# Bible/commentary JSON is gitignored (too large for git), we must list excludes
# here explicitly — otherwise Vercel would fall back to .gitignore and drop all
# of the corpus, shipping a data-less site.

# Build & dev artifacts (Vercel rebuilds remotely)
node_modules
.next
.vercel

# Secrets — provided via Vercel project env, never uploaded
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# CORPUS CDN payoff (docs/CORPUS_CDN_DESIGN.md §4.4/A6, plan 2026-08-13). The static corpus now
# ships from Vercel Blob (see next.config.ts rewrites, gated on CORPUS_CDN_BASE) rather than the
# deploy bundle — proven live 2026-08-15: 24,992 files synced, parity checked (200 sampled fetches
# hash-verified), the flip deployed and a real content file confirmed served through the app at
# https://ancientpaths.app/commentaries/1ch/1.json. The predeploy gate still reads these directories
# from LOCAL DISK for its licensing/identity checks (Gate B, corpus-identity legs, the freshness leg
# added by this project) — .vercelignore only controls what `vercel --prod` UPLOADS, so those checks
# are unaffected. Rollback: delete these three lines (and unset CORPUS_CDN_BASE) to return to
# shipping the corpus in the bundle, byte for byte as before this project.
#
# This SUPERSEDES the old per-chapter-Bible-only exclusion below (which existed only to stay under
# Vercel's 15,000-file CLI limit) — the whole corpus leaves the bundle now, so that narrower carve-out
# is redundant but left in place as a no-op belt-and-suspenders in case CORPUS_CDN_BASE is ever unset
# without also reverting this block.
public/bible/
public/commentaries/
public/original/

# Per-CHAPTER Bible JSON: superseded by per-book files at public/bible/<t>/<book>.json.
# Excluded so the deploy stays under Vercel's 15,000-file CLI limit. The per-book
# .json files (two levels deep) and all commentaries are still uploaded.
public/bible/*/*/
